  "term": "risk ratio",
  "definition": "A risk ratio is a number used to compare how likely an outcome is in one group versus another. In this context, an adjusted risk ratio shows that after accounting for other factors, values above 1 indicate higher risk in the group being examined compared with the reference group.",
